{"title":"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be fixed <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Natural_numbers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Natural numbers\">positive numbers</a>. For each <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real number</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/52500fa910532c875ed622e3f6b55a4398add5d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_t, y_t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex\" title=\"Vertex\">vertex</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parabola\" title=\"Parabola\">parabola</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d17cdd68de54bd20830f1b670649db2524666c05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=ax^2+tx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" />. If the set of the vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/52500fa910532c875ed622e3f6b55a4398add5d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_t, y_t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> for all real numbers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is graphed on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cartesian_plane\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cartesian plane\">plane</a>, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Graph\" title=\"Graph\">graph</a> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f622c7b3b0527ef26d6da6b321eeaceeff7c0cc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\text{a straight line} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\text{a parabola} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\text{part, but not all, of a parabola} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\text{one branch of a hyperbola} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"824\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/403931d1321daa791c4064ef5cc19d8ce70a3d24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\text{None of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/59335b242eaf2d5fca91f549b3bee34dc49bbfbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2 + tx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c538269a5b7ee5c4f0d3879a26a8b38cd07ca8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{t}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"39\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41b948f20d5faee83a505f32ddd1162f715b7325.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_t=-\\frac{t}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />. Substituting yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46d618ec55ae0d8ad027f880e43520384e56218a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_t=-\\frac{t^2}{4a^2}+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"41\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/2044cfd369d73869ca985b68c6e36b7c4b8ac98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_t=-\\frac{t^2}{4a^2}+c=-a(-\\frac{t}{2a})^2+c=-ax_t^2+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"348\" height=\"41\" />, so all of the vertices are on a parabola. However, we have only showed that all of the points in the locus of vertices are on a parabola, we have not shown whether or not all points on the parabola are on the locus. Assume we are given an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/4485828f5a19c01ef573976d83d057fa840ed1e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> on the parabola. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/7/1c7e3bad78cc3b2a62326ed9218c53648eec64c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{t}{2a}=x_t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/9/f790410751c244583ea3e57913a77cd0e95df2a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = -2ax_t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" />, so a unique <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, and therefore a unique vertex, is determined for each point on the parabola. We therefore conclude that every point in the locus is on the parabola and every point on the parabola is in the locus, and the graph of the locus is the same as the graph of the parabola, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0d5b8fdfd2bd98c8be0bad569663660c33f3438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{B}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME\" title=\"1984 AHSME\">1984 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1984 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1984\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_A